		<title>Our Jobs</title>
		<link>http://localhost/?page_id=86661</link>
		<pubDate>Sat, 27 Dec 2014 20:05:10 +0000</pubDate>
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Zoe Hu]]></dc:creator>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">http://www.thegazelle.org/?page_id=86661</guid>
		<description></description>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[&nbsp;

<a href="http://thegazelle.s3.amazonaws.com/gazelle/2014/12/11_30_GLOBAL_Plottel_0.jpg"><img class="wp-image-86921 size-full" style="width: 100%;" src="http://thegazelle.s3.amazonaws.com/gazelle/2014/12/11_30_GLOBAL_Plottel_0.jpg" alt="11_30_GLOBAL_Plottel" width="1200" height="406" /></a>
<span style="text-align: center; font-size: 12.5px; color: #ccc;"> Illustration by Megan Eloise/The Gazelle</span>

&nbsp;
<p style="text-align: center;"><strong>In addition to our staff writer, photographer and illustrator spots (which are always up for 
grabs), there are several available editing positions at The Gazelle for the upcoming year.
Check out the details below; we'd love for you to join us.</strong></p>

<p style="text-align: center;"><strong> All applications due by Jan. 12.</strong></p>
&nbsp;
<ul class="nav nav-tabs" style="width: 80%; margin: auto;">
	<li class="active"><a href="#managing" data-toggle="tab">Managing Editor</a></li>
	<li><a href="#creatived" data-toggle="tab">Creative Editor</a></li>
	<li><a href="#deputynews" data-toggle="tab">Deputy News</a></li>
	<li><a href="#deputyfeatures" data-toggle="tab">Deputy Features</a></li>
	<li><a href="#deputyopinion" data-toggle="tab">Deputy Opinion</a></li>
	<li><a href="#columnist" data-toggle="tab">Columnists</a></li>
	<li><a href="#howto" data-toggle="tab">Apply</a></li>
</ul>
<div class="tab-content" style="height: inherit; width: 80%; margin: auto;">
<div id="managing" class="tab-pane fade active in">
<div class="media"><a class="pull-left" style="padding: 0 4%;" href="#">
<img class="media-object" src="http://thegazelle.s3.amazonaws.com/gazelle/2014/12/gaz-logo.jpg" alt="" width="150" height="150" />
</a>
<div class="media-body" style="padding-top: 3%;">
<h4 class="media-heading">What it is</h4>
<p dir="ltr" style="padding-right: 8%;">The ME sits on The Gazelle’s management team, which is its core leadership team. The ME brainstorms for, organizes and oversees publication with the Editors-in-Chief and has particular influence in shaping the culture and content of The Gazelle.</p>

<div class="media-body" style="padding-top: 2%;">
<h4 class="media-heading">Responsibilities</h4>
<p dir="ltr" style="padding-right: 8%;">The ME attends The Gazelle's two weekly meetings — pitch and budget meetings — as well as editing sessions on Saturday production nights. However, in keeping with more of a management and leadership position, the ME is also about being a voice of reason and using a critical eye to keep The Gazelle on track, calling for change when needed. The ME works closely with the management team to plan ahead for The Gazelle.</p>

</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div id="creatived" class="tab-pane fade in">
<div class="media"><a class="pull-left" style="padding: 0 4%;" href="#">
<img class="media-object" src="http://thegazelle.s3.amazonaws.com/gazelle/2014/12/gaz-logo.jpg" alt="" width="150" height="150" />
</a>
<div class="media-body" style="padding-top: 3%;">
<h4 class="media-heading">What it is</h4>
<p dir="ltr" style="padding-right: 8%;">This position will lead The Gazelle's Creative desk, a new venture dedicated to showcasing and supporting NYUAD student artwork such as poetry, short story, film, photography, music, graphic design and other creative endeavors. Every two weeks, the desk will review submissions of student work and choose one piece to publish, alongside an optional Q&A with the student artist. The desk aims to serve as both archive and platform, where students may discuss, inspire and be inspired. </p>

<div class="media-body" style="padding-top: 2%;">
<h4 class="media-heading">Responsibilities</h4>
<p dir="ltr" style="padding-right: 8%;">The Creative editor will lead the desk's team, guiding a rotating panel in its selection of the bi-weekly published work. The Creative editor will also be responsible for co-ordinating Q&As, which may be written by the editor or another member of the desk. A large part of the job will involve outreach - encouraging students to submit their work and thinking outside the box in terms of what the Creative desk can include. How could we publish spoken word poetry? What other examples of student creativity can we showcase? The Creative editor will attend two meetings every two weeks - one for the piece selection and the other for production.</p>

</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div id="deputynews" class="tab-pane fade in">
<div class="media"><a class="pull-left" style="padding: 0 4%;" href="#">
<img class="media-object" src="http://thegazelle.s3.amazonaws.com/gazelle/2014/12/gaz-logo.jpg" alt="" width="150" height="150" />
</a>
<div class="media-body" style="padding-top: 3%;">
<h4 class="media-heading">What it is</h4>
<p dir="ltr" style="padding-right: 8%;">This deputy works under the News editor to help pitch story ideas for the desk, keeping up-to-date with news both on campus and off.</p>

<div class="media-body" style="padding-top: 2%;">
<h4 class="media-heading">Responsibilities</h4>
<p dir="ltr" style="padding-right: 8%;">The News deputy stays in touch with the editor to manage News stories throughout the week, looking out for possible pitches and often working with authors to shape an article. The News deputy edits on Saturday production nights until all articles in the desk are ready for publication - usually three to five articles per week. The News deputy comes to weekly pitch meetings to provide ideas for upcoming stories and also consistently writes for the desk.</p>

</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div id="deputyfeatures" class="tab-pane fade in">
<div class="media"><a class="pull-left" style="padding: 0 4%;" href="#">
<img class="media-object" src="http://thegazelle.s3.amazonaws.com/gazelle/2014/12/gaz-logo.jpg" alt="" width="150" height="150" />
</a>
<div class="media-body" style="padding-top: 3%;">
<h4 class="media-heading">What it is</h4>
<p dir="ltr" style="padding-right: 8%;">The Features deputy helps the Features team, in support of the editor, to find stories and co-ordinate articles for the desk. Features articles usually mean in-depth looks into certain elements of the NYUAD or Abu Dhabi experience — ranging from event nights to cafeteria food to doorknobs — and how they affect members in the community. The desk requires a keen eye on what interests the reader and how to investigate those topics in new ways.</p>

<div class="media-body" style="padding-top: 2%;">
<h4 class="media-heading">Responsibilities</h4>
<p dir="ltr" style="padding-right: 8%;">The Features deputy keeps in communication with the editor to manage Features stories throughout the week, often checking in with authors and making sure articles stay on track for publication. The Features deputy edits on Saturday production nights until all articles in their desk are ready for publication - usually three to six articles per week. The Features deputy comes to weekly pitch meetings to provide ideas for upcoming stories and also consistently writes for the desk.</p>

</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div id="deputyopinion" class="tab-pane fade in">
<div class="media"><a class="pull-left" style="padding: 0 4%;" href="#">
<img class="media-object" src="http://thegazelle.s3.amazonaws.com/gazelle/2014/12/gaz-logo.jpg" alt="" width="150" height="150" />
</a>
<div class="media-body" style="padding-top: 3%;">
<h4 class="media-heading">What it is</h4>
<p dir="ltr" style="padding-right: 8%;">The deputy helps the Opinion editor compile Opinion articles every week for the latest issue. A large part of the role requires staying in touch with interesting and controversial topics on campus, seeking out diverse voices and asking potential writers to contribute (and then badgering those writers to turn in their articles when they're running behind schedule).</p>

<div class="media-body" style="padding-top: 2%;">
<h4 class="media-heading">Responsibilities</h4>
<p dir="ltr" style="padding-right: 8%;">The Opinion deputy communicates with the Opinion editor to organize articles throughout the week, keeping up with controversial new topics that are dominating conversation (or Facebook fights) among the NYUAD community. The Opinion deputy edits on Saturday production nights until all Opinion articles are ready for publication — usually two to four articles per week. The deputy also writes for the desk, and may keep up a column if they have a special interest or focus.</p>

</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div id="columnist" class="tab-pane fade in">
<div class="media"><a class="pull-left" style="padding: 0 4%;" href="#">
<img class="media-object" src="http://thegazelle.s3.amazonaws.com/gazelle/2014/12/gaz-logo.jpg" alt="" width="150" height="150" />
</a>
<div class="media-body" style="padding-top: 1%;">
<h4 class="media-heading">What it is</h4>
<p dir="ltr" style="padding-right: 8%;">Calling all Facebook ranters, soapbox shouters, dinner table debaters and preachers with no choir: if you have a passion — whether it be human rights law or the political implications of break-dance — give your friends' ears a break and come write about it for us.

The Gazelle is looking for a handful of individuals to keep columns under our Opinion Desk, where writers will provide analysis and critique on any topic of their choosing. Doesn't have to be a cohesive theme; your focus can be as broad as 'the intersection of religion and youth,' 'start-ups' or even 'cosmopolitanism.' We just ask that you write consistently and persuasively.</p>

<div class="media-body" style="padding-top: 2%;">
<h4 class="media-heading">Responsibilities</h4>
<p dir="ltr" style="padding-right: 8%;">One opinion article on a weekly or bi-weekly basis.</p>

</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div id="howto" class="tab-pane fade in">
<div class="media"><a class="pull-left" style="padding: 0 4%;" href="#">
<img class="media-object" src="http://thegazelle.s3.amazonaws.com/gazelle/2014/12/gaz-logo.jpg" alt="" width="150" height="150" />
</a>
<div class="media-body" style="padding-top: 1%;">
<h4 class="media-heading">Shoot us an email</h4>
<p dir="ltr" style="padding-right: 8%;">
To apply, send an email to zh415@nyu.edu or jpb443@nyu.edu with the subject line 'Gazelle App' and the following reqs:
<ul><ul>What position(s) you're interested in
Two or three lines on why you'd be a good fit
Two ideas for articles or photo essays that could be published by The Gazelle
At least two links to the best articles, photo essays or documentaries you liked this past month
</ul></ul>
Thanks, and we hope to hear from you soon! 
</p>

</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>]]></content:encoded>
