	<item>
		<title>Hassan Syed</title>
		<link>http://localhost/?p=391</link>
		<pubDate>Fri, 08 Feb 2013 21:01:23 +0000</pubDate>
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Alistair Blacklock]]></dc:creator>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">http://web.thegazelle.org/hassan-syed</guid>
		<description></description>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[<br /><em>Hassan Syed was unavailable for interview at time of publication.</em><br /><p>The role of the Senator of the Student Government is to liaise with representatives from various entities within the UAE and the GNU regarding the interests of students of NYU Abu Dhabi. Having been born and raised in the Emirates to Pakistani and Emirati parents, I have at times experienced both the life of an expatriate and that of a UAE national. As such, I believe I’m well suited for the role of Senator as I can immerse myself in the local culture and can effectively advocate the interests of students and the NYUAD community. If elected, I aspire to initiate a conference for various Student Governments within the UAE, hosted by NYUAD, to be able to exchange ideas on student governance. This is in line with my vision of setting up NYU Abu Dhabi as the regional leader in Student Governance! I feel that my experience as the Operations intern at the Career Development Center has already allowed me to develop a strong interpersonal relationship with the people within the various departments that are key to ensuring that the Senator can perform his duties as necessary. If you catch me around, ask me about my plans for the Student Government! </p>]]></content:encoded>
