	<item>
		<title>Andres Rodriguez</title>
		<link>http://localhost/?p=111</link>
		<pubDate>Sat, 09 Feb 2013 18:54:24 +0000</pubDate>
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Maitha Al Mansoori]]></dc:creator>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">http://web.thegazelle.org/andres-rodriguez</guid>
		<description></description>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[<br /><p>After fencing his way through high school and becoming part of the national fencing team in San José, Costa Rica, Andres Rodriguez’s new target is the student government.</p><p>

Rodriguez, who was originally born in Mexico, travelled to many places such as Sudan, Nicaragua, Cuba and France. He grew up in Costa Rica where he attended high school before moving to NYUAD.</p><p>

He once participated in the fencing youth world cup in Arizona and the Central American Championship in Nicaragua. Through participating in athletic SIGs, he has continued his passion for fencing.</p><p>

Rodriguez also aspires to be a part of the student government at NYUAD. He has worked with the parliamentary advisory board and attended general assemblies to keep up with the university’s affairs.</p><p>

“Working with [the parliamentary advisory board] really taught me a lot in terms of how the student government is run, how decisions are made and the needs of students,” Rodriguez said.</p><p>

If elected, Rodriguez seeks to work closely with the staff and groups within the student body, such as the technology group to create an app for the bus schedule, and to connect the students more to the Abu Dhabi community. </p>]]></content:encoded>
