	<item>
		<title>Leah Reynolds</title>
		<link>http://localhost/?p=231</link>
		<pubDate>Sat, 09 Feb 2013 19:12:48 +0000</pubDate>
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Joey Bui]]></dc:creator>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">http://web.thegazelle.org/leah-reynolds</guid>
		<description></description>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[<br /><p>Leah Reynolds is always thinking about how to unify people. She brings students together as a leader in various SIGs and NYUAD Spiritual Life. Before finals, bringing food and pillows to crowded study rooms is her mark of camaraderie. From organizing Christian Fellowship events, Reynolds has connected people from all walks of life in the wider Abu Dhabi community. Her candidate platform is focused on strengthening the NYUAD community, especially for incoming classes and for students studying abroad.</p><p>

At the same time, Reynolds is driven by the individuals around her. Of the NYUAD community, she is convinced that each person has an interesting story to tell and a talent to be revealed. She wants to create more opportunities for NYUAD students to tell their stories and show their abilities, to “tap into the things that make people special,” she said. When she worked on a committee to discuss school values, Reynolds emphasized the importance of representing the great differences of this diverse community.</p><p>

Beyond achievements on paper, Reynold’s inclination toward actively assembling students while still seeing each person as an individual, suggests the kind of student government president she hopes to be. Reynolds is the person that connects people and gives them opportunities. She is also the kind of person offering Sweethearts to her visitors and even more when they leave to bring them back for their roommates. </p>]]></content:encoded>
