	<item>
		<title>Andrew Pitts</title>
		<link>http://localhost/?p=261</link>
		<pubDate>Sat, 09 Feb 2013 19:38:17 +0000</pubDate>
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Clare Hennig]]></dc:creator>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">http://web.thegazelle.org/andrew-pitts-platform</guid>
		<description></description>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[<br /><p>It’s a hard thing to run for office. You have to put yourself out there. Here I am: My name is Andrew, I’m a junior, a philosophy and literature major, and the colour of my beard does not match the colour of my hair. For me, this school is everything. If I hadn’t come to NYUAD I
have no idea what I would have done. I’ll go right out there and say it: This school has come a long way, in three short years we have gone from being nothing to a real living and breathing community. However, that journey is far from over. I truly believe that NYUAD has the potential to revolutionize the way education is viewed throughout the world. </p><p>However, while ‘well begun is half-way done’ we still have so much left to do.
We have a choice before us, will this NYU Abu Dhabi experiment be looked back on as founded with the right intentions but never actualized, or will people look back and only see our success. Right now, complacency is the enemy we have to continue striving forward in order for the NYU Abu Dhabi experiment to change the world.</p>]]></content:encoded>
