		<title>Clara Correia</title>
		<link>http://localhost/?p=341</link>
		<pubDate>Sat, 09 Feb 2013 19:56:09 +0000</pubDate>
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Nina Bayatti]]></dc:creator>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">http://web.thegazelle.org/clara-correia-platform</guid>
		<description></description>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[<br /><p>When I applied to NYUAD, I knew that one of the differentials of this university is the amount of resources that students have access to. Being part of this fairly new Student Body gives all of us a great leeway to engage in the creation and development of various projects, namely the Student Interest Groups.</p><p>
It is with this in mind that I would like to be vested the position of Alternate-Senator, and
to continue to create a space where students can enjoy from this resourceful environment
to the favor of the community. Thus, I am fully committed to enabling SIG to develop their potentialities while maintaining clear guidelines, efficient and transparent communication and accountability.</p><p>
I hope work together with the Student Government in tackling the issues that are brought by the community, and in perpetuating the open environment for dialogue and close collaboration between administration, faculty and students as we move forward in the year.</p>]]></content:encoded>
