	<item>
		<title>Veronica Houk</title>
		<link>http://localhost/?p=361</link>
		<pubDate>Sat, 09 Feb 2013 20:00:07 +0000</pubDate>
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Alistair Blacklock]]></dc:creator>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">http://web.thegazelle.org/veronica-houk-platform</guid>
		<description></description>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[<br /><p>Due to NYUAD’s youth and developing character, its Student Government has
the heightened opportunity and responsibility to influence the school’s growth, strength, and integrity. The University’s previous student administrations made commitments
to a democratic representation of the student body and its wishes, the establishment of Student Government’s roles and responsibilities, and open communication throughout the Global Network University. I am dedicated not only to continuing these legacies but also
to creating a unified framework for traditions, procedures, and collaborations within the University. This structure will provide precedent for future governments as well as foster Student Governments based on partnership rather than individuals or discrete committees and boards.</p><p>
As Secretary, I will contribute to a proactive, forthright leadership that will
cultivate an environment in which students continue to have a voice in policy, events, and student life. I invite the NYUAD student body to join me in this vision.</p>]]></content:encoded>
