	<item>
		<title>TGTV: Gender values and cultural difference in Abu Dhabi</title>
		<link>http://localhost/?p=21551</link>
		<pubDate>Sun, 27 Oct 2013 03:31:53 +0000</pubDate>
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[TGTV]]></dc:creator>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">http://www.thegazelle.org/?p=21551</guid>
		<description></description>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[TGTV is a student-led, widely broadcasted, uncensored debate amongst the individuals of NYU Abu Dhabi and the global network at NYU — students, faculty, administrators­ and staff — who would not normally have access to one another.

It seeks to explore complicated, controversial topics regarding the global community, and the role this community plays on a larger scale. The opinions expressed in each episode are of guests and not those of The Gazelle.

This episode features Carlos Guedes, associate professor of music, Mohamed Amine Belarbi, NYUAD sophomore and Nafisatou Mounkaila, NYUAD freshman. The discussion is about gender roles and cultural difference in Abu Dhabi.

[embed width="640" height="480"]http://youtu.be/b22FrvNWOto[/embed]]]></content:encoded>
