		<description></description>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[TGTV is a student-led, widely broadcasted, uncensored debate among the individuals of NYU Abu Dhabi and the Global Network University at NYU — students, faculty, administrators­ and staff — who would not normally have access to one another.

It seeks to explore complex, controversial topics regarding the global community and the role this community plays on a larger scale. The opinions expressed in each episode are of guests and not those of The Gazelle.

This episode features four NYUAD students: senior Charlotte Wang, junior Corey Meyer, junior Amel Yagoub and sophomore Rodrigo Ceballos. The discussion focuses on the presence and perception of the United States at NYUAD.

[embed width="640" height="480"]http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZIgyC9cZ2tA&amp;feature=youtu.be[/embed]]]></content:encoded>
