	<item>
		<title>TGTV: Keeping it P.C. </title>
		<link>http://localhost/?p=29491</link>
		<pubDate>Mon, 25 Nov 2013 03:40:06 +0000</pubDate>
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[TGTV]]></dc:creator>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">http://www.thegazelle.org/?p=29491</guid>
		<description></description>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[TGTV is a student-led, uncensored debate among the individuals of NYU Abu Dhabi and the global network university.

It seeks to explore complex, controversial topics regarding the global community. The opinions expressed in each episode are of guests and do not reflect those of The Gazelle.

This episode features three students: NYUAD senior Joshua Shirley, NYUNY junior Alexa Singh and NYUAD freshman Sam Ball.  The discussion focuses on political correctness and to the extent we ought to be politically correct at NYUAD and the global network at large.

[embed width="640" height="480"]http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Wu2Ep5SQYq4&amp;feature=youtu.be[/embed]

&nbsp;

<em> Correction: In the video, we misspell Alice Sholto-Douglas' name in the final credits. We regret this error.</em>]]></content:encoded>
