	<item>
		<title>New Campus, New Faces</title>
		<link>http://localhost/?p=67611</link>
		<pubDate>Mon, 15 Sep 2014 15:58:16 +0000</pubDate>
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Sebastian Rojas Cabal]]></dc:creator>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">http://www.thegazelle.org/?p=67611</guid>
		<description></description>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p style="font-size:1.5em;text-align:center;"><em>Click on each member of staff's name to view quotes from them.</em></p>
<br>
<div style="display: inline-block;">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="https://s3.amazonaws.com/gazelle_ad/meet-new-staff/meetnewstaff.css">
      <div id="donna" class="option-box col-md-6">
          <img class="img-responsive" src="https://s3.amazonaws.com/gazelle_ad/meet-new-staff/donna.png" alt="">
          <button type="button" class="btn staff-button btn-lg" id="donna-button">Donna Eddleman</button>
        <div class="quote-box">
          <div class="title"><strong>Deputy Dean of Students</strong></div>
          <div class=start-quote-mark>“</div><p>I expect to be exposed to different ways of seeing the world, which I believe will be humbling, enlightening and enriching. I am sure, given that I have never lived outside the United States, I will make some mistakes, but hope that people will be patient when I stumble and help me to learn and to grow at NYUAD.</p>
          <p>An opportunity to support the academic mission of the University by bringing to life the lessons of the classroom and by teaching students valuable life lessons that will aid them in their success long after they graduate.</p>
          <p>I want to establish strong and valuable partnerships with faculty so that together we can develop intentional and meaningful student experiences.</p>
          <p>I want to to help students to dream big and to realize their untapped potential.</p><div class=end-quote-mark>”</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div id="doug" class="option-box col-md-6"><img class="img-responsive" src="https://s3.amazonaws.com/gazelle_ad/meet-new-staff/doug.png" alt="">
        <button type="button" class="btn staff-button btn-lg" id="doug-button">Doug Cutchins</button>
        <div class="quote-box">
          <div class="title"><strong>Director of Global Awards, Career Development Center</strong></div>
          <div class=start-quote-mark>“</div><p>I leapt at the opportunity to come to NYUAD because my life's work is connecting with exceptionally talented young people, helping them realize who they are and what they are passionate about, and then linking them to international opportunities to help them realize their potential. Where else would I have a chance to work with some of the very best students, who come here from all over the world, all in an entrepreneurial setting where we have the chance to be daring and bold?</p><div class=end-quote-mark>”</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div id="peter" class="option-box"><img class="img-responsive" src="https://s3.amazonaws.com/gazelle_ad/meet-new-staff/peter.png" alt="">
        <button type="button" class="btn staff-button btn-lg" id="peter-button">Peter Smith</button>
        <div class="quote-box">
          <div class="title"><strong>Swim Coach, Athletics</strong></div>
          <div class=start-quote-mark>“</div><p>My expectations here at NYUAD are to help provide … the students with an awesome experience and long lasting memories of their life at university, as well as develop life skills in swimming and water confidence. With the new campus and facilities this should be [an] enjoyable journey. What I want to achieve whilst here is to become a valuable member of the Athletics department and help develop a strong swim program for our students and to finally develop a swim squad for representation against other institutions.</p><div class=end-quote-mark>”</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div id="alta" class="option-box"><img class="img-responsive" src="https://s3.amazonaws.com/gazelle_ad/meet-new-staff/alta.png" alt="">
        <button type="button" class="btn staff-button btn-lg" id="alta-button">Alta Mauro</button>
        <div class="quote-box">
          <div class="title"><strong>Director of Intercultural Education &amp; Spiritual Life</strong></div>
          <div class=start-quote-mark>“</div><p>I expect to engage phenomenal students with a range of interests, skills, and passions in critical, progressive, sometimes-difficult-but-always-worthwhile conversations about who they are, where they are from, what they know and believe, and who we all are together.</p>
          <p>Intercultural education is a community goal, and therefore must be a community responsibility. I hope to engage as many members of our campus community in contemplation about intercultural competence, and to support students, staff, and faculty in determining authentic ways for them to contribute to an evolving conversation about related issues.</p><div class=end-quote-mark>”</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div id="heather" class="option-box"><img class="img-responsive" src="https://s3.amazonaws.com/gazelle_ad/meet-new-staff/heather.png" alt="">
        <button type="button" class="btn staff-button btn-lg" id="heather-button">Heather Lortie</button>
        <div class="quote-box">
          <div class="title"><strong>Special Projects Coordinator, Intercultural Education &amp; Spiritual Life, Community Outreach</strong></div>
          <div class=start-quote-mark>“</div><p>I expect to be immersed in the culture of the UAE and the multiculturalism of NYUAD, to share opportunities [and] to notice, reflect, think critically and, ultimately, to be deeply affected by interactions with thoughtful students and colleagues whose experiences, values, and views may be fundamentally different from my own.</p>
          <p>Both the university and Alta have set broad and ambitious goals for this new department. Fostering intercultural [competence] is central to NYUAD’s mission. One core principle that I learned as an educator and psychotherapist, which feels counter-intuitive at times, is the notion that when doing complex, transformative work, slower is faster. As eager and committed as we all are to building a more united, generous, and responsive world, this may be a perfect time for our community to slow down, individually and collectively. I hope to contribute by holding open a strong, safe space where everyone feels free to join the process in ways that feel authentic and true.</p><div class=end-quote-mark>”</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div id="tina" class="option-box"><img class="img-responsive" src="https://s3.amazonaws.com/gazelle_ad/meet-new-staff/tina.png" alt="">
        <button type="button" class="btn staff-button btn-lg" id="tina-button">Tina Wadhwa</button>
        <div class="quote-box">
          <div class="title"><strong>Wellness Counsellor, Health and Wellness Center</strong></div>
          <div class=start-quote-mark>“</div><p>I am thrilled to be a part of the Health and Wellness Center here at NYU Abu Dhabi. I come here via NYU New York’s Counseling and Wellness Services, where I gained a strong understanding of the complex mental health challenges college students face.</p>
          <p>College can often be a time of personal and academic growth, which can be accompanied by unwanted growing pains! These growing pains can present themselves in a wide-range of issues - from sleep difficulties and feelings of homesickness, to more significant mental health needs ... Whatever your need may be - or if you just want a safe space to explore – we welcome you to utilize the counseling center!</p><div class=end-quote-mark>”</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div id="shaffer" class="option-box" style="margin-left: 25%;"><img class="img-responsive" src="https://s3.amazonaws.com/gazelle_ad/meet-new-staff/shaffer.png" alt="">
        <button type="button" class="btn staff-button btn-lg" id="shaffer-button">Jennifer Shaffer</button>
        <div class="quote-box">
          <div class="title"><strong>Physical Education Curriculum Coordinator, Athletics</strong></div>
          <div class=start-quote-mark>“</div><p>I expect to grow and develop as an educator and soccer coach. I am excited to meet the students and [members of the] NYUAD community from all over the world and learn about what experiences they bring to Abu Dhabi.</p>
          <p>I would like to deliver a quality physical education program to the NYUAD students and grow the program as the campus grows. I hope that all students experience new physical activities and are motivated to be healthy and fit for a lifetime.</p><div class=end-quote-mark>”</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <script type="text/javascript" src="https://s3.amazonaws.com/gazelle_ad/meet-new-staff/meetnewstaff.js"></script>
</div>
<div>
<p>NYU Abu Dhabi’s transition to its new campus in Saadiyat Island has triggered changes in various university departments for the 2014-15 academic year. The various offices at NYUAD prepared during the summer to welcome incoming and returning students to a university with enhanced facilities and new programs.</p>

<p>Campus Life have benefitted from the transition as it allows them to offer more resources to students. In an email to The Gazelle, Assistant Dean of Campus Life Renee Dugan enumerates the new spaces in the Campus Center that allow them to provide better services to students.</p>

<p>“The NEST where students can come for help with equipment, SIG funding or tickets; and a dedicated multi-faith space that can be used for a variety of programming, including prayer, meditation, dialogue, and spiritual celebrations. The Activity Zone will be a central place for students to hang out and play games," Dugan wrote.</p>

<p>Interim Medical Director at the Health and Wellness Center Dr. Tehmina Kazmi also wrote to The Gazelle explaining that the change in venue has provided more and improved exam and counseling rooms. She also followed up on the process of finding someone to replace former director Dr. Birgit Pols, who <a href="http://www.thegazelle.org/issue/38/news/hwc/">left</a> toward the end of the Spring semester.</p>

<p>“We are working closely with human resources in the process of hiring more staff, doctors, nurses and counselors. As far as the director position, as you know I am serving as the Interim Medical Director and will do so until a permanent replacement has been hired,” Dr. Kazmi explained.</p>

<p>Although new and improved facilities have sparked enthusiasm amongst incoming and returning students, Director of Athletics Peter Dicce made clear that not all the sports venues would be functional this semester. In an email to The Gazelle, Dicce outlined the times at which the various facilities will be available.</p>

<p>“Access to fully functional sports facilities will be staged throughout the Fall semester with the pool, multipurpose room, tennis courts and outdoor fields/track coming online. By the spring semester we will have full access,” Dicce said.</p>

<p>But changes go beyond facilities, as can be noted from the expectations of the new staff. An example of this expansion is the Career Development Center, which is working to enhance their services in terms of advising students on fellowships and awards. Student Life, on the other hand, is developing stronger programs to promote intercultural understanding.</p>
</div>
&nbsp;

<em style="font-size:1.2em;">Sebastian Rojas Cabal is the news editor. Email him at src441@nyu.edu</em>]]></content:encoded>
