		<description></description>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[&nbsp;

[caption id="attachment_66391" align="alignnone" width="1200"]<a href="http://thegazelle.s3.amazonaws.com/gazelle/2014/03/andres.jpg"><img class="size-full wp-image-66391" src="http://thegazelle.s3.amazonaws.com/gazelle/2014/03/andres.jpg" alt="Courtesy of Student Government " width="1200" height="599" /></a> <em>Courtesy of Student Government</em>[/caption]
<h3>Class of 2018 Class Representative: Max Eckert</h3>
Number of votes: 53

Freshman Max Eckert wrote in his platform: “I can represent and encourage growth between our freshman year. I will be at every meeting, and I assure you – there will never be a bad time to talk to me, give me a suggestion or voice a concern.”

<em> </em>
<h3><b>Class of 2017 Class Representative: King-him Joseph Chu</b></h3>
Number of votes: 79

Sophomore Joseph Chu wrote to The Gazelle, “I'm really thankful for all my class's support that they've given me and I look forward to working with you all to make this semester the best and most enjoyable for us that it can possibly be.”

<em> </em>
<h3><b>Class of 2016 Class Representative: Haya Raef</b></h3>
Number of votes: 52

Junior Haya Raef wrote to The Gazelle: “Thank you to all the juniors for being so supportive and letting me represent our wonderful class. I look forward to an exciting semester with will you all, filled with  events and activities that will bring our class together and leave us with great memories.”

<em> </em>
<h3><b>Class of 2015 Class Representative: Corey Meyer</b></h3>
Number of votes: 68

Senior Corey Meyer wrote to The Gazelle: “I am absolutely humbled by this opportunity to continue serving my classmates. Thank you all so much for your unending support and I look forward to making our final year the best one yet. As always, feel free to contact me about any concerns you may have.”

<em> </em>

<em>Andres Rodriguez is editor in chief. Email him at the gazelle.org@gmail.com</em>

&nbsp;]]></content:encoded>
