		<description></description>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[<iframe width="853" height="480" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/eQ-ZqrNdFis" frameborder="0"  allowfullscreen="allowfullscreen"></iframe>

Members of the NYU Abu Dhabi community share their thoughts on the recent Human Rights Watch <a href="http://www.thegazelle.org/issue/56/news/response/">report</a> that investigated labor abuse on Saadiyat. Some offer new perspectives, others reiterate old concerns. The Gazelle's Video Desk looked at how this select group, though not representative of the university, interacted with labor on Saadiyat in ways that are telling of the intersection between the issue and everyday life at NYU Abu Dhabi. ]]></content:encoded>
