		<content:encoded><![CDATA[On 10 March, sophomore Moe al Blooshi, also known as Auden, began a 21-hour long performance art piece in which he scrubbed the ground of Saadiyat campus while wearing a kandura.

His work was selected to be featured as part of an ongoing initiative, run by The Gazelle's Creative Desk, to create space for student artwork.

If you'd like to learn more about this week's artist, check out the podcast interview, which was conducted, produced and edited by creative editor Laura Waltje.

