		<title>Artist: Julia Zhao Xu</title>
		<link>http://localhost/?p=100601</link>
		<pubDate>Sat, 14 Mar 2015 23:03:41 +0000</pubDate>
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Laura Waltje]]></dc:creator>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">http://www.thegazelle.org/?p=100601</guid>
		<description></description>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[[caption id="attachment_100721" align="alignnone" width="910"]<a href="http://thegazelle.s3.amazonaws.com/gazelle/2015/03/Plantmeunderatree1.jpg"><img class="size-full wp-image-100721" src="http://thegazelle.s3.amazonaws.com/gazelle/2015/03/Plantmeunderatree1.jpg" alt="Graphic by Eve Hamel-Smith/TheGazelle" width="910" height="512" /></a> Graphic by Eve Hamel-Smith/TheGazelle[/caption]

Julia Zhao Xu's work was selected to be published as part of an ongoing initiative, run by The Gazelle's Creative Desk, to create a space for student artwork. If you'd like to learn more about this week's artist, check out the podcast interview, which was conducted, produced and edited by creative editor Laura Waltje.

[powerpress channel="creative"]

&nbsp;

<strong>When I Die, Plant Me Under a Tree </strong>

by Julia Xu

&nbsp;

When I die, plant me under a tree.

The earthworms wriggle through my ribs.

The decaying cells stiffen to wax.

&nbsp;

When I die, plant me under a tree.

Fertilize new life.

Grow new branches.

&nbsp;

When I die, plant me under a tree.

I live in a box erected by my mind all my life.

I want none in death.

&nbsp;

When I die, plant me under a tree.

That returns oxygen to the world

For all the carbon dioxide I have breathed.

&nbsp;

When I die, plant me under a tree.

The atoms that once were me

Can be free, whistling in the wind.

&nbsp;

The Creative Desk publishes one work per week selected by a rotating panel. We are looking for prose, poetry, photography, film, visual arts, music and more. Send your creative work to ljw296@nyu.edu. Submissions accepted on a rolling basis.

<em>This week's artwork was selected by creative editor Laura Johanna Waltje, Isabella Peralta, Nadeen Alalami, and deputy news editor Oliver Andersson Hugemark. Email them at feedback@gzl.me.</em>]]></content:encoded>
