		<content:encoded><![CDATA[[caption id="attachment_108031" align="alignnone" width="1200"]<a href="http://thegazelle.s3.amazonaws.com/gazelle/2015/04/04_11_Features_Playlist2.jpg"><img class="size-full wp-image-108031" src="http://thegazelle.s3.amazonaws.com/gazelle/2015/04/04_11_Features_Playlist2.jpg" alt="Graphic by Mariko Kuroda/TheGazelle" width="1200" height="678" /></a> <em>Graphic by Mariko Kuroda/TheGazelle</em>[/caption]

From Moroccan Shilha poetry to Lebanese music longing for an idealized past, this playlist, inspired by the Arab Culture Night held at NYU Abu Dhabi this April, celebrates music and artists from all walks of the Middle East. Inclusive of non-Arab minorities. 

Listen to the full playlist <a href="https://8tracks.com/thegazellead/arab-cultural-night-playlist">here</a>.

<h3>Aleb </h3>by Yasmine Hamdan, Lebanon

<h3>Kol Maoul Touba</h3>by Abdel Halim Hafez, Egypt

<h3>Roo7 Blade </h3>by Toot Ard, Syrian Golan Heights

<h3>Fog el Nakhal </h3>by Hiba Mansouri, Kuwait

<h3>Jabal </h3>by Safar Barlik, Lebanon

<h3>Jibal Alnuba</h3>by Débruit &amp; Alsarah, France and Sudan

<h3>Izenzaren Chamekh</h3>by Elhaj Belaïd, Morocco

<h3>Ara Salmou</h3>by Soap Kills, Lebanon

<h3>Warni Warni </h3>by Omar Souleyman, Syria

<h3>Eskat El Nezam </h3>by Zeid Hamdan, Lebanon

<h3>Sweet Temptress</h3>by Bei Ru, LA-based

<h3>Ana Moush Kafir</h3>by Ziad Rahbani, Lebanon

<h3>Hasna Ya Layla </h3>by Djamel Laroussi, Algeria

<h3>Al Shaky </h3>by Hussain Al Jasmi, The UAE

<em>Sala Shaker is a contributing writer. Email her at feedback@gzl.me.</em>]]></content:encoded>
