	<item>
		<title>A playlist: IranTalks</title>
		<link>http://localhost/?p=115311</link>
		<pubDate>Sat, 25 Apr 2015 21:38:37 +0000</pubDate>
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Sala Shaker]]></dc:creator>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">http://www.thegazelle.org/?p=115311</guid>
		<description></description>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[[caption id="attachment_115381" align="aligncenter" width="797"]<a href="http://thegazelle.s3.amazonaws.com/gazelle/2015/04/playlist.png"><img src="http://thegazelle.s3.amazonaws.com/gazelle/2015/04/playlist-797x430.png" alt="Graphic by Mariko Kuroda, edited by Zoë Hu" width="797" height="430" class="size-thumbnail wp-image-115381" /></a>[/caption]

Iran, or more specifically, its nuclear program, has been at the forefront of international news headlines recently, given the ongoing negotiations on the country’s nuclear activities.This playlist aims to transcend a purely political approach to Iran and shift the focus away from the country’s politics to its people, as everyone ought to know about <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/No_One_Knows_About_Persian_Cats">Persian Cats</a>.

Listen to the full playlist <a href="http://8tracks.com/thegazellead/iran-deal-mix">here</a>.

<h3>Gole Yakh</h3> Kouroush Yaghmaei
<h3>Fastalgia</h3> Moslem Rasouli
<h3>Be Qarda</h3> Ali Reza & Haj Ghorban Soleymani  
<h3>Littles</h3> Raks Raks Raks (Fatemah Sultan) 
<h3>Darya Toufan</h3> Ahmad Ashourpour 
<h3>Drunk with love</h3> Rana Farhan 
<h3>Jouwani (feat. Bahman Ghobadi)</h3> Mahdyar Aghjani 
<h3>Leila</h3> Kourosh Yaghmaei 
<h3>Naz Kardanet Vaveyla</h3> Sima Bina 
<h3>Nu</h3> Man O To
<h3>Gahzal Shakeri</h3> Man O To

<em>Sala Shaker is a music editor. Email her at feedback@gzl.me.</em>]]></content:encoded>
