	<item>
		<title>In Photos: Annual Flea Market</title>
		<link>http://localhost/?p=118871</link>
		<pubDate>Sat, 09 May 2015 20:49:08 +0000</pubDate>
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Karma Gurung]]></dc:creator>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">http://www.thegazelle.org/?p=118871</guid>
		<description></description>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[[slideshow][Photo courtesy of Karma Gurung](http://thegazelle.s3.amazonaws.com/gazelle/2015/05/05_10_Features_Fleamarket.jpg);[Photo courtesy of Karma Gurung](http://thegazelle.s3.amazonaws.com/gazelle/2015/05/05_10_Features_Fleamarket2.jpg);[Photo courtesy of Karma Gurung](http://thegazelle.s3.amazonaws.com/gazelle/2015/05/05_10_Features_Fleamarket3.jpg);[Photo courtesy of Karma Gurung](http://thegazelle.s3.amazonaws.com/gazelle/2015/05/05_10_Features_Fleamarket4.jpg);[Photo courtesy of Karma Gurung](http://thegazelle.s3.amazonaws.com/gazelle/2015/05/05_10_Features_Fleamarket5.jpg);[/slideshow]

Organized by Community Life, the annual Flea Market signalled the end of another academic year. The market provided a great opportunity for all to visit, regardless of interest. It was set up in the East Forum of the Campus Center and drew a large crowd of NYU Abu Dhabi students, staff members and faculty, as well as people outside of the community. 

Similarly, the table holders ranged from professional artists to fellow students wanting to get rid of some belongings before the summer. Baked goods, clothing items, electronic gadgets, paintings and handmade jewelry were among the items sold in the market. At the end of the room, a large pile of free clothes was set up, drawing the most attention. 

An option to leave plants for the summer was also available for those who wished to.

<em>Karma Gurung is deputy news editor. Email her at feedback@gzl.me.</em>]]></content:encoded>
