		<description></description>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[Sophomore Andrija Klaric experiments with different music effects and genres that range from classical guitar music to experimental, electronic music. His tracks have elements of rock, industrial music, and "pick and choose ingredients from all over the place." His work spans a wide spectrum of soundscapes, from technical experiments to full-fledged songs.
<h3>Gravedigger</h3>
<iframe src="https://w.soundcloud.com/player/?url=https%3A//api.soundcloud.com/tracks/195998067&amp;color=ff5500&amp;auto_play=false&amp;hide_related=false&amp;show_comments=true&amp;show_user=true&amp;show_reposts=false" width="100%" height="166" frameborder="no" scrolling="no"></iframe>
<h3>Xenomorph</h3>
<iframe src="https://w.soundcloud.com/player/?url=https%3A//api.soundcloud.com/tracks/163565588&amp;color=ff5500&amp;auto_play=false&amp;hide_related=false&amp;show_comments=true&amp;show_user=true&amp;show_reposts=false" width="100%" height="166" frameborder="no" scrolling="no"></iframe>

If you'd like to listen to more of Andrija's tracks, check out his Soundcloud <a href="https://soundcloud.com/peoplemachine" target="_blank">page</a>. To learn more about his work as an artist, listen to the podcast below. [powerpress channel="creative"]

&nbsp;

Andrija Klaric's work was selected to be published as part of an ongoing initiative, run by The Gazelle’s Creative Desk, to create a space for student artwork. The Creative Desk publishes works selected by a rotating panel. We are looking for prose, poetry, photography, film, visual arts, music and more.

Send your creative work to bfp226@nyu.edu or nk1389@nyu.edu. Submissions are accepted on a rolling basis.

<em>This week’s artwork was selected by creative editor Isabella Peralta, deputy creative editor Natalie Kopczewski, Melinda Szekeres, Adam Ashraf and Roland Folkmayer. </em><em>Email them at feedback@thegazelle.org.</em>]]></content:encoded>
