		<description></description>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[Freshman Arthur de Oliveira is an aspiring filmmaker who uses his emotions as catalysts and inspiration for writing and directing short films. 

Preferring to leave interpretation open to the viewer, Oliveira incorporates a variety of camera angles and objects to tell his story, while always including an element of mystery. 

<h3>Short Film: Blue</h3>

<iframe src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/MoaV46TK10Q" width="853" height="480" frameborder="0" allowfullscreen="allowfullscreen"></iframe>


To learn more about his work as an artist, listen to the podcast below. [powerpress channel="creative"]

&nbsp;

Arthur de Oliveira's work was selected to be published as part of an ongoing initiative, run by The Gazelle’s Creative Desk, to create a space for student artwork. The Creative Desk publishes works selected by a rotating panel. We are looking for prose, poetry, photography, film, visual arts, music and more.

Send your creative work to bfp226@nyu.edu. Submissions are accepted on a rolling basis.

<em>This week’s artwork was selected by creative editor Natalie Kopczewski. Email her at feedback@thegazelle.org.</em>]]></content:encoded>
