	<item>
		<title>Souks, Knafeh and Jordanian Arabic</title>
		<link>http://localhost/?p=138711</link>
		<pubDate>Tue, 20 Oct 2015 00:11:56 +0000</pubDate>
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Clare Hennig]]></dc:creator>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">http://www.thegazelle.org/?p=138711</guid>
		<description></description>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[Over the past long weekend, the NYU Abu Dhabi Arabic department organized a class trip to Jordan. Two dozen of the students enrolled in Intermediate Arabic I and II, Advanced Arabic I and Palestinian Dialect classes flew out on Wednesday night to experience three days of Jordanian language, culture and food.

Highlights of the trip included a visit to the Citadel overlooking the city of Amman, shopping in the downtown souks, a short climb up Mount Nebo, an afternoon sunbathing at the Dead Sea, chatting with Jordanian language peers and, of course, non-stop immersion in Arabic.

