	<item>
		<title>JUICE HACKS: 5 NEW FIVE-A-DAYS TO TRY AT THE MARKETPLACE</title>
		<link>http://localhost/?p=139241</link>
		<pubDate>Sat, 31 Oct 2015 14:12:32 +0000</pubDate>
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Melinda Szekeres]]></dc:creator>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">http://www.thegazelle.org/?p=139241</guid>
		<description></description>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[With a special issue on health, here are even more juice hacks to add in The Gazelle’s growing <a href="http://www.thegazelle.org/issue/65/features/juice/">list</a> of smoothie recipes. All of these can be created using ingredients available at the Goodness Me counter at Marketplace as Five-a-Day orders, or with a bit more extra preparation in the comfort of your dorms, homes or apartments.

<h3>Not So Fast, Piña Colada</h3>

[big_image]<a href="http://thegazelle.s3.amazonaws.com/gazelle/2015/10/Juice-2-copy.jpg"><img class="aligncenter size-thumbnail wp-image-141091" src="http://thegazelle.s3.amazonaws.com/gazelle/2015/10/Juice-2-copy-860x319.jpg" alt="Juice 2 copy" width="860" height="319" /></a>[/big_image]

Unlike its cocktail inspiration, this pineapple drink won’t send you spinning; with juice based ingredients, it stays refreshing and light. The basil leaves bring out even more flavor.

If you prefer thicker and richer, it is possible to add coconut powder as an alternative to the coconut milk that has been discontinued from Goodness Me.

<h3>Hang On, This Smoothie is Avo-Control</h3>

[big_image]
</b><a href="http://thegazelle.s3.amazonaws.com/gazelle/2015/10/Juice-3-copy.jpg"><img class="aligncenter size-thumbnail wp-image-141101" src="http://thegazelle.s3.amazonaws.com/gazelle/2015/10/Juice-3-copy-860x320.jpg" alt="Juice 3 copy" width="860" height="320" /></a>[/big_image]

Many people seem to take out the avocados in the available Go Green juices or just don't get that available smoothie because the overall combination does not do justice to all of the flavors. So, here is a recipe — with green apple, mint leaves and ginger — that brings out the thick richness of avocado. 

Ask for whole green apples to be blended instead of just juice, and if asked for a choice of liquids, request apple juice to supplement. This drink is great to get in between classes for that extra boost of energy.

<h3>Off To The Tropics</h3>

[big_image]<a href="http://thegazelle.s3.amazonaws.com/gazelle/2015/10/Untitled-2-copy.jpg"><img class="aligncenter size-thumbnail wp-image-141111" src="http://thegazelle.s3.amazonaws.com/gazelle/2015/10/Untitled-2-copy-860x319.jpg" alt="Untitled-2 copy" width="860" height="319" /></a>[/big_image]

This coral pink mix is created with six ingredients, but those working the counter are usually lenient enough to let you get away with it. 

The zingy flavor of the ginger and mint is balanced out with honey for a super smooth finish. This inspired combination will leave your friends speechless at your juicing abilities.

<h3>I'm Not Like the Other Green Drinks</h3>

[big_image]<a href="http://thegazelle.s3.amazonaws.com/gazelle/2015/10/More-Juice-2-copy.jpg"><img class="aligncenter size-thumbnail wp-image-141121" src="http://thegazelle.s3.amazonaws.com/gazelle/2015/10/More-Juice-2-copy-860x319.jpg" alt="More Juice 2 copy" width="860" height="319" /></a>[/big_image]

If you like that tangy, strong taste after orange juice, this green smoothie is for you. The drink, adopted from a juice bar combination spotted in Prague, will give you the satisfaction of a striking aftertaste while also mixing in both spinach and kale.

<em>All graphics by Melinda Szekeres. Melinda Szekeres is a copy editor. Email her at feedback@thegazelle.org. </em>]]></content:encoded>
